body:
This fallback drops property validators when `IModelMetadataProvider` is decorated:

```csharp
sealed class MetadataDecorator(IModelMetadataProvider inner) : IModelMetadataProvider
{
    public ModelMetadata GetMetadataForType(Type type) => inner.GetMetadataForType(type);

    public IEnumerable<ModelMetadata> GetMetadataForProperties(Type type) =>
        inner.GetMetadataForProperties(type);
}

sealed class LengthUnion(string value) : IUnion
{
    [MaxLength(3)]
    public object Value => value;
}
```

With that decorator registered, validating `new LengthUnion("long")` used to report a `Value` error. It now replaces the property metadata with plain `string` metadata, drops `[MaxLength]`, and accepts the value.

The synthetic entry bypasses the container's property validation filter:

```csharp
[ValidateNever]
sealed class SuppressedUnion : IUnion
{
    object IUnion.Value => throw new InvalidOperationException("Getter must not run.");
}
```

Validating `new SuppressedUnion()` did not invoke the getter before this change. It now throws because the synthetic `object` type metadata has no property filter and bypasses the class-level `[ValidateNever]`.

Separately, the Minimal API source appears to have two union-validation gaps. Neither is introduced by this PR or needs to block the MVC fix:

```csharp
[SkipValidation]
public sealed class IgnoredCase
{
    [Range(1, 10)]
    public int Count { get; init; }
}

public sealed class CheckedCase
{
    [Range(1, 10)]
    public int Count { get; init; }
}

public union Command(IgnoredCase, CheckedCase);
public union Batch(CheckedCase[], bool);
```

- `new Command(new IgnoredCase { Count = 0 })` should be accepted, but union-case discovery doesn't honor the case's `[SkipValidation]`. The `CheckedCase` alternative should still be validated.
- `new Batch(new[] { new CheckedCase { Count = 0 } })` should report `Value[0].Count`, but collection traversal checks the declared `Value` type (`object`) and misses the array's elements.

These are source-traced, not executed repros. The original generator support issue ([#68268](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68268)) is closed, and I didn't find dedicated issues for these cases. Worth tracking separately if they aren't already covered elsewhere?
